marching:
Pictures pass me in long review,--
Marching columns of dead events.
I was tender, and, often, true;

maria:
The Pitti’s palace-front is drawn in fire;
And, past the quays, Maria Novella’s Place,
In which the mystic obelisks stand up

margin:
No name writ on it—poems, by the form;
Some Greek upon the margin,—lady’s Greek,
Without the accents. Read it? Not a word.

marbles:
Little boys turned in their sleep and smiled,
Dreaming of marbles, dreaming of agates;
Little girls leapt from their beds to see

marvel:
Extract of that same root;
Why marvel at the hectic blood
That flushes this wild fruit?

martyrs:
Slaying with sabre-stroke bloody and fell;
Born where the heroes and martyrs were dying,
Torn by the fury of bullet and shell.

mary's:
Who yet would count adulteries on her beads
At holy Mary’s shrine, and never blush;
Because the saints are so far off, we lose

marian:
Sing Rachel, sing May;
Only Marian cannot sing
While her sweetheart's away.

mares:
ah despair,
still fate tricked our mares,
for they swerved,

marvelous:
Straight by the plumb-line's shivering length;
Make my marvelous wall so thick
Dead nor living may shake its strength.

mart:
The soul’s Rialto hath its merchandize;
I barter curl for curl upon that mart,
And from my poet’s forehead to my heart

Bought to-night, possessed, and tossed
Back to the mart again to-morrow,
Worth and over, what you cost;

marge:
I think the hemlock likes to stand
Upon a marge of snow;
It suits his own austerity,

marfy:
Dey's Allen on de hillside,
An' Marfy in de plain;
Fu' Christmas was like springtime,

marred:
With snails and slugs in corners out of sight;
I never marred the curious sudden stool
That perfects in a night.

marrowless:
A being has the same;
A marrowless assembly
Is culpabler than shame.

martyrdoms:
To Peter then, He speaks to us the same;
The word suits many different martyrdoms,
And signifies a multiform of death,

marquisate:
And, after seven, I might consider it,
For there’s some comfort in a marquisate
When all’s said,—yes, but after the seven years;

margins:
And, while with their spondaic prodigious mouths
They lap the lucent margins as babe-gods,
Proclaims them bastards. Wolff’s an atheist;
